id: ops-bun-negative-extglobs
title: Native Bun path.matchesGlob rejects negative extglob duplication scopes
description: "Bun 1.3.5 implements node:path.matchesGlob with different negative-extglob behavior from Node. The new dependency-free duplication matcher passes all six pinned filesystem contracts on Node, while a direct bun test run fails the negative-extglob assertion. Documented consumer duplication launchers use Node; native Bun packed acceptance passes for default globs. Track native Bun custom-pattern parity separately."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T04:47:00.429Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T04:47:00.429Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce the matcher difference using real filesystem fixtures and both runtimes.; Preserve dependency-free source discovery and unchanged 100% coverage thresholds while establishing native Bun negative-extglob parity or an explicit unsupported-pattern diagnostic.; Retain Node filesystem contracts and packed npm/native Bun default-glob clean and duplicate controls.
repro_steps: "Compare matchesGlob(\"xsrc/xa.ts\", \"xsrc/x!(z|ambient.d).ts\") using node --input-type=module -e and bun --eval, then run node --test test/duplication-glob.test.ts and bun test test/duplication-glob.test.ts."
expected_result: "Native Bun and Node accept the same configured negative-extglob scope, or the runtime refuses unsupported scope explicitly before scanning."
actual_result: Node matches the source and all six contracts pass; Bun returns false and five of six contracts pass. Default packed npm and native Bun duplication gates both pass.
